{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"call_8f8235f92e6c9450","type":"tool_result","content":"        optimized_call = make_copy_and_call(\n            sym_tensor_indices, input_buffers, runtime_callable\n        )\n    else:\n        optimized_call = runtime_callable\n\n    fn = VllmSerializableFunction(\n        **state,\n        optimized_call=optimized_call,\n        vllm_backend=None,\n    )\n    return fn\n\n\n# Source directories whose *contents* change which ops/aten calls Dynamo\n# traces into the forwarded graph, without appearing in the traced-file set\n# recorded by an AOT artifact: the quantized-linear kernel registry\n# (`kernels/linear/**`), the quant methods' `process_weights_after_loading`\n# layout contracts (`layers/quantization/**`) and the MoE backend oracle\n# (`layers/fused_moe/oracle/**`).\n#\n# Enabling a (model, backend) combo by swapping a kernel implementation --\n# e.g. registering a BF16-dequant FP8 kernel on GPUs without hardware FP8 --\n# edits exactly these files and none of the traced model files. See\n# `_kernel_selection_hash` below for why that poisons the compile cache.\n_KERNEL_SELECTION_DIRS: tuple[str, ...] = (\n    \"model_executor/kernels\",\n    \"model_executor/layers/quantization\",\n    \"model_executor/layers/fused_moe/oracle\",\n)\n\n\n@functools.lru_cache(maxsize=1)\ndef _kernel_selection_hash() -> str:\n    \"\"\"Digest of the kernel/quant-layout sources that shape the traced graph.\n\n    The AOT compile-cache key (`aot_compile_hash_factors`) covers the env,\n    the VllmConfig and the model's forward function, and\n    `_verify_source_unchanged` additionally re-checks the *traced* files\n    recorded inside an existing artifact. Neither covers a very common class\n    of change: a source edit that only alters *which* implementation gets\n    traced, e.g. a kernel-registry / backend-selection patch.\n\n    Concretely, when a patch makes a linear layer dequantize its FP8 weight to\n    BF16 [N, K] at load time, the traced model files are untouched, so the\n    stale artifact (built for an FP8 [K, N] `aten._scaled_mm`) still verifies\n    and is reloaded. It then calls its hard-coded `_scaled_mm` with the wrong\n    tensor layout and dies in `profile_run` with::\n\n        AssertionError: expected size 2560==4096, stride 4096==1 at dim=0 ...\n\n    even though the eager (uncompiled) path would have run fine. Hashing these\n    sources makes any such patch change the cache key, forcing a correct\n    recompile instead of a silent stale-graph replay.\n\n    Returns an empty string (i.e. contributes nothing) if the sources cannot be\n    read, so a failure here can never block startup.\n    \"\"\"\n    try:\n        root = os.path.dirname(os.path.dirname(os.path.abspath(__file__)))\n        hasher = hashlib.sha256()\n        paths: list[str] = []\n        for rel_dir in _KERNEL_SELECTION_DIRS:\n            abs_dir = os.path.join(root, rel_dir.replace(\"/\", os.sep))\n            if not os.path.isdir(abs_dir):\n                continue\n            for dirpath, _dirnames, filenames in os.walk(abs_dir):\n                for name in filenames:\n                    if name.endswith(\".py\"):\n                        paths.append(os.path.join(dirpath, name))\n        for path in sorted(paths):\n            hasher.update(os.path.relpath(path, root).encode())\n            try:\n                with open(path, \"rb\") as f:\n                    hasher.update(f.read())\n            except OSError as exc:  # pragma: no cover - unreadable file\n                logger.debug(\"compile-cache: skipping %s: %s\", path, exc)\n                hasher.update(b\"<unreadable>\")\n        return hasher.hexdigest()\n    except Exception as exc:  # pragma: no cover - never block startup\n        logger.warning(\"compile-cache: kernel-selection hash unavailable: %s\", exc)","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4398ab91-ecaa-4257-90d2-2cd3a9bc7624","uuid":"